$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>We see that only the statements $\\neg (X \\lor \\neg Y)$ and $\\neg X \\land Y$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.</p>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is &quot;II and III only&quot;.</p>\n","topic":{"id":2821,"name":"Logical Equivalence"},"example":{"id":13224,"title":"Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"},"group":{"id":26154,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253417,"answer":{"id":62318128,"cread":"2026-10-16T03:49:18.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15310},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62318138,"created":"2026-10-16T03:49:32.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":9807,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 3:49 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:10","question":{"id":127969,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":13224,"text":"<p>Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?</p>\n<ol class=\"questionStatements\"><li>  $\\neg Q \\land (P \\lor Q)$ </li><li>  $P  \\land  \\neg  Q$ </li><li>  $\\neg P \\land \\neg Q$ </li></ol>","choice1":"I and II only\n","choice2":"I and III only\n","choice3":"\nNone of those listed","choice4":"I, II, and III\n","choice5":"II and III only","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:</p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,P\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,Q\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, \\neg Q \\land (P \\lor Q) \\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,P  \\land  \\neg  Q \\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\neg P \\land \\neg Q\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p>We see that only the statements $\\neg Q \\land (P \\lor Q)$ and $P  \\land  \\neg  Q$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.</p>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is &quot;I and II only.&quot;</p>\n","topic":{"id":2821,"name":"Logical Equivalence"},"example":{"id":13224,"title":"Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"},"group":{"id":26155,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14253417,"answer":{"id":62318138,"cread":"2026-10-16T03:49:32.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":9807},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62318157,"created":"2026-10-16T03:50:02.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[1,0,0,0]","timeElapsed":25190,"number":4,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 3:50 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:25","question":{"id":182515,"format":"SS","difficulty":1,"exampleId":13223,"text":"<p>Find the missing values in the following truth table:</p>\n","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, let&#39;s solve for the missing values:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>When $A \\equiv \\textrm T$ and $B \\equiv \\textrm T,$ we have\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\neg A \\land  B &\\equiv \\neg \\textrm T \\land  \\textrm T \\\\[3pt]\n&\\equiv \\textrm F \\land \\textrm T \\\\[3pt]\n&\\equiv \\textrm F\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>When $A \\equiv \\textrm T$ and $B \\equiv \\textrm F,$ we have\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\neg A \\land  B &\\equiv \\neg \\textrm T \\land  \\textrm F \\\\[3pt]\n&\\equiv \\textrm F \\land \\textrm F \\\\[3pt]\n&\\equiv \\textrm F\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>When $A \\equiv \\textrm F$ and $B \\equiv \\textrm T,$ we have\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\neg (A \\lor \\neg B) &\\equiv \\neg (\\textrm F \\lor \\neg \\textrm T) \\\\[3pt]\n&\\equiv \\neg (\\textrm F \\lor \\textrm F) \\\\[3pt]\n&\\equiv \\neg \\textrm F\\\\[3pt]\n&\\equiv \\textrm T\n\\end{align*} \n\\]\nOur completed table is shown below.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\neg (A \\lor \\neg B) \\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, \\neg A \\land B \\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td> \n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</table> \n\n<p>To determine whether $\\neg (A \\lor \\neg B) $ is logically equivalent to $\\neg A \\land B,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.</p>\n<p>Looking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\textrm{F},\\textrm{F},\\textrm{T},\\textrm{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that </p>\n<p>\\[\n\\neg (A \\lor \\neg B)  \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\equiv}\\neg A \\land B.\n\\] </p>\n","topic":{"id":2821,"name":"Logical Equivalence"},"example":{"id":13223,"title":"Identifying Equivalent Statements Using Partially Completed Truth Tables"},"group":{"id":26151,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":{"segments":[{"text":"<table rules=\"all\" cellpadding=\"10\" align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n<td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\neg (A \\lor \\neg B) \\,$</td>\n<td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, \\neg A \\land B \\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\"